# Sage-A1.5 (InternScience / Shanghai AI Lab, released 2026-10-15, Apache-2.0),
# an agentic fine-tune of Qwen3.6-35B-A3B: MoE 35B total / 3B active,
# Qwen3_5MoeForConditionalGeneration, 40 layers of which 10 hold KV
# (Gated DeltaNet elsewhere), 2 KV heads x head_dim 256 -> 10 KiB/token at fp8.
# Official weights are BF16 (72 GB) and FP8 (35 GB): neither fits one 32 GB
# 5090, so this is cyankiwi's AWQ-INT4 g32 (the same quantizer as the
# Qwen3.6 and Qwen3.8 checkpoints this stack already ran), pinned to revision
# 12e664cc. It keeps the experts of layers 0 and 39, the shared experts, the
# DeltaNet and attention projections and the vision tower at BF16 (28.4 GB on
# disk incl. the unused MTP head). Single-GPU only: one card serves it, GPU 1
# stays free for the second engine.
# Needs vLLM >= 0.32 (Qwen3.6-family kernels on sm_120); runs on the 0.33.0
# venv, see VLLM_VENV. Serve flags from the official model card:
# --reasoning-parser qwen3 --enable-auto-tool-choice --tool-call-parser qwen3_coder;
# --language-model-only drops the vision encoder (the card's text-only mode),
# which the chat path never feeds, and returns its memory to the KV pool.
MODEL_SLUG=sage-a1.5
MODEL_ID=cyankiwi/Sage-A1.5-AWQ-INT4
MODEL_DIR=sage-a1.5-awq-int4
MODEL_NAME=sage-a1.5
MODEL_DESC="Sage-A1.5 (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B agentic fine-tune, MoE 35B / 3B active, AWQ-INT4 g32, 64k ctx, text-only)"
HF_EXCLUDE="figures/*"
VLLM_VENV=/opt/munin/services/vllm-0.33.0/venv
VLLM_QUANTIZATION=compressed-tensors
VLLM_KV_CACHE_DTYPE=fp8
VLLM_TOOL_PARSER=qwen3_coder
VLLM_REASONING_PARSER=qwen3
VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS="--language-model-only"
VLLM_GPU_MEM_UTIL=0.90
VLLM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=65536
VLLM_MAX_NUM_SEQS_SINGLE=2
# Single-GPU profile; TP=2 was not measured for this model.
VLLM_MAX_NUM_SEQS_TP2=2
LLM_THINKING_MODE=enable_thinking
# The Sage chat template has no effort kwarg (only enable_thinking and the
# opt-in `verification` flag); send none.
LLM_REASONING_EFFORT=
KV_KIB_PER_TOKEN=10
# The model card's recommended sampling (temperature 1.0, top_p 0.95, top_k 20,
# min_p 0, presence_penalty 1.5, repetition_penalty 1.0); the code profile keeps
# the Qwen3.6 code-persona values, the card gives no separate set.
SAMPLING_DEFAULT='{"temperature": 1.0, "top_p": 0.95, "top_k": 20, "min_p": 0.0, "presence_penalty": 1.5}'
SAMPLING_CODE='{"temperature": 0.6, "top_p": 0.95, "top_k": 20, "min_p": 0.0, "presence_penalty": 0.0}'
